the medical facility individual annual rate cap is 360, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(B)(i)".

the medical facility couple both in facility annual rate cap is 720, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(B)(iii)".

the publicly operated community residence resident limit is 16, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(C)".

the emergency shelter eligibility month limit is 6, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(D)".

the emergency shelter lookback period months is 9, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(D)".

the temporary institutionalization month limit is 3, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(G)(i)".

the timely inmate reporting payment amount is 400, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(I)(i)(II)".

the later inmate reporting payment amount is 200, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(I)(i)(II)".

the timely inmate reporting deadline days is 15, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(I)(i)(II)".

the later inmate reporting deadline days is 90, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(I)(i)(II)".

the duplicate reporting payment reduction rate is 0.5, as stated in "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(I)(ii)".

rule qualifying_publicly_operated_community_residence with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(C)":
a person is qualifying publicly operated community residence if
    the residence of the person is publicly operated community residence
    and the residence number of residents of the person is a number N
    and the publicly operated community residence resident limit is a number M
    and N <= M.

rule inmate_of_public_institution_for_subparagraph_a with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(A), (C)":
a person is inmate of public institution for subparagraph_a if
    the person is inmate of public institution throughout month
    and it is not the case that the person is qualifying publicly operated community residence.

rule public_emergency_shelter_eligibility_exception_applies with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(D)":
the public emergency shelter eligibility exception of a person applies if
    the person is resident of public emergency shelter for homeless throughout month
    and the months eligible by reason of public emergency shelter in current nine month period of the person is a number N
    and the emergency shelter eligibility month limit is a number M
    and N < M.

rule retained_benefit_institutional_month_eligibility_applies_1 with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(E)":
the retained benefit institutional month eligibility of a person applies if
    the person is inmate of public institution primarily for medical or psychiatric care throughout month
    and the person was eligible under section 1382 h_a or b for preceding month
    and the person is institution or facility agreement permits retention of benefit payable by reason of subparagraph e
    and the month of the person is initial or succeeding month for continuing subparagraph e institution or facility status.

rule retained_benefit_institutional_month_eligibility_applies_2 with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(E)":
the retained benefit institutional month eligibility of a person applies if
    the person is in medical treatment facility throughout month
    and the person was eligible under section 1382 h_a or b for preceding month
    and the person is institution or facility agreement permits retention of benefit payable by reason of subparagraph e
    and the month of the person is initial or succeeding month for continuing subparagraph e institution or facility status.

rule temporary_institutionalization_exception_applies_1 with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(G)":
the temporary institutionalization exception of a person applies if
    the person is inmate of public institution primarily for medical or psychiatric care throughout month
    and the person is physician certifies stay likely not to exceed temporary institutionalization month limit
    and the month number in continuous institutionalization period of the person is a number N
    and the temporary institutionalization month limit is a number M
    and N <= M
    and the person needs to maintain home or living arrangement expenses for return.

rule temporary_institutionalization_exception_applies_2 with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(G)":
the temporary institutionalization exception of a person applies if
    the person is in medical treatment facility receiving medicaid or child private health insurance payments throughout month
    and the person is physician certifies stay likely not to exceed temporary institutionalization month limit
    and the month number in continuous institutionalization period of the person is a number N
    and the temporary institutionalization month limit is a number M
    and N <= M
    and the person needs to maintain home or living arrangement expenses for return.

rule public_institution_inmate_ineligible_for_month with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(A), (B), (D), (E), (G)":
a person is public institution inmate ineligible for month if
    the person is inmate of public institution for subparagraph_a
    and it is not the case that the person is in medical treatment facility receiving payments under subparagraph b throughout month
    and it is not the case that the public emergency shelter eligibility exception of the person applies
    and it is not the case that the retained benefit institutional month eligibility of the person applies
    and it is not the case that the temporary institutionalization exception of the person applies.

rule medical_facility_annual_benefit_payable with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(B)":
the medical facility annual benefit payable of a person is an amount N if
    the retained benefit institutional month eligibility of the person applies
    and N = 0
    otherwise the temporary institutionalization exception of the person applies
    and N = 0
    otherwise the person is a person
    and it is not the case that the person is in medical treatment facility receiving payments under subparagraph b throughout month
    and N = 0
    otherwise the individual of the person has eligible spouse
    and the spouse of the person is in medical treatment facility throughout month
    and the medical facility couple both in facility annual rate cap is an amount M
    and the combined income not excluded pursuant to section 1382 a b of the person is an amount K
    and a number P = M - K
    and the maximum of 0 and P is N
    otherwise the individual of the person has eligible spouse
    and the medical facility individual annual rate cap is an amount Q
    and the individual income not excluded pursuant to section 1382 a b of the person is an amount R
    and the statutory base annual rate without eligible spouse is an amount S
    and the spouse income not excluded pursuant to section 1382 a b of the person is an amount T
    and a number U = Q - R
    and the maximum of 0 and U is a number V
    and a number W = S - T
    and the maximum of 0 and W is a number X
    and N = V + X
    otherwise the medical facility individual annual rate cap is an amount Y
    and the individual income not excluded pursuant to section 1382 a b of the person is an amount Z
    and a number C = Y - Z
    and the maximum of 0 and C is N.

rule not_treated_as_eligible_under_section_1382h_for_subparagraph_e_preceding_month_test with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(F)":
a person is not treated as eligible under section 1382 h for subparagraph e preceding month test if
    the retained benefit institutional month eligibility of the person applies.

rule temporary_institutionalization_benefit_payable_at_prior_month_rate with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(G)":
the temporary institutionalization benefit payable at prior month rate of a person is an amount N if
    the temporary institutionalization exception of the person applies
    and the benefit rate applicable in month prior to first full month in institution or facility of the person is a number M
    and the maximum of 0 and M is N
    otherwise the person is a person
    and N = 0.

rule inmate_reporting_payment_to_institution with provenance "42 USC 1382(e)(1)(I)(i)(II), (ii)":
the inmate reporting payment to institution of a person is an amount N if
    the person is a person
    and it is not the case that the institution of the person has agreement to report inmates to commissioner
    and N = 0
    otherwise the person is a person
    and it is not the case that the individual of the person received benefit under this subchapter for month preceding first full month of confinement
    and N = 0
    otherwise the person is a person
    and it is not the case that the person is commissioner determines individual ineligible by reason of confinement based on institution information
    and N = 0
    otherwise the person is a person
    and the days after inmate entry when information furnished of the person is a number M
        and the timely inmate reporting deadline days is a number K
        and M <= K
        and the timely inmate reporting payment amount is an amount P
        otherwise the days after inmate entry when information furnished of the person is a number Q
        and the later inmate reporting deadline days is a number R
        and Q <= R
        and the later inmate reporting payment amount is P
        otherwise P = 0
    and the person is commissioner also required to pay institution under section 402 x 3 B for same individual
        and the duplicate reporting payment reduction rate is a rate S
        otherwise S = 1
    and N = P * S.

